@@ -46,3 +46,13 @@ LaunchAgent 名称为 `com.jacky.relationship-advisor`。安装记录与当前 r
 重新启动：`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.jacky.relationship-advisor`。
 
 修改公网入口时，在该 LaunchAgent 的 `EnvironmentVariables` 中设置 `ADVISOR_ORIGIN`，重新加载后校验 HTTPS 登录、Cookie 和流式回答。邀请码保持 `000000`。
+
+## Paws engine and model selection
+
+Protocol 3 devices support Codex (gpt-6-astra, gpt-6.1-sol, gpt-6-sol, gpt-6-luna) and Claude Code (Sonnet, Opus, Haiku) from the composer. Account permissions still determine model availability. The hosted service remains fixed to Codex / gpt-6-astra. There is no automatic engine or model fallback.
+
+Existing Codex-only grants require fresh consent to use Claude. Upgrading retains the old connection in tab-scoped sessionStorage; the connection manager can switch back to its history. Forgetting connections, logging out, or closing the tab clears these credentials under the existing storage policy. Scoped read-only history links remain separate and support both wire versions.
+
+Deploy the Paws app-chat-models migration, server, client and protocol 3 daemon before rebuilding this site's SDK with `PAWS_WORKSPACE=<checkout> node scripts/build-paws-sdk.mjs`. The restricted Claude runtime uses the device's native login/API and dedicated proxy/CA configuration; tools, MCP, plugins and project configuration are disabled.
+
+For isolated browser regression, run `PAWS_WORKSPACE=<checkout> node test/fixtures/model-browser.mjs`. It prints a loopback URL; all credentials and model replies in this fixture are fake. Production acceptance still requires real accounts and the deployed delegation chain.
